# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREDENTIALS — never commit these
#
# .env holds the Alpaca API keys, the Anthropic key, the Pushover tokens
# and the Telegram bot token. Anything matching .env* stays out, including
# the dated backups, because a leaked backup leaks exactly as much as a
# leaked original. .env.example below is the safe, empty template.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIVE STATE — machine-specific, changes every cycle
#
# These describe what LOCKBOT is doing right now on THIS machine. Tracking
# them would mean a merge conflict on every cycle and, worse, restoring an
# old commit would restore a stale idea of which positions are open. The
# broker is the source of truth for state, not the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
position_state.json
options_position_state.json
risk_state.json
options_risk_state.json
notification_state.json
notifications_state.json
lockbot_heartbeat.json
self_repair_state.json
self_repair_test.json
scanner_state.json
hud_voice_state.json
performance_metrics.json

# Old copies of live state. Superseded by git history and never useful to
# restore — the broker decides what is actually open.
*_OLD.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA AND LOGS
#
# Trading history and logs are records, not source. signals.csv alone is
# 7 MB and grows every scan; committing it would bloat the repository
# without making anything reproducible. Keep them on disk, out of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.csv
*.jsonl
*.zip
lockbot_log.txt
paper_order_log.txt
!requirements*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKUPS
#
# The 26 hand-made backup copies this repository replaces. They are
# committed once in the initial commit so nothing is lost, then removed
# from the working tree — git is the history from here on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.bak2_*
*.bak3_*
*.corrupt_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYTHON
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDITOR AND OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPORT BUNDLES AND GENERATED REPORTS  (added 2026-08-19)
#
# solas_handover/ is a point-in-time copy of the source, made to onboard
# another agent. It is already stale -- its options_contracts.py is 921
# lines against 1,121 live -- and on 2026-08-19 it polluted a grep for the
# debit-cap defect, returning the old code as though it were running.
#
# This is the *_OLD / *_backup / *_v0_N problem the project deliberately
# removed on 2026-08-06. Git holds the history those copies were standing
# in for. Regenerate the bundle when it is needed; never track it.
solas_handover/
options_tradeable_*.csv
options_tradeable_latest.txt
watchdog.log
config_sweep_state.json
rule_registry_state.json
rule_registry.jsonl
